1}, {"text": "out of control and are considered a feral species detrimental to the natural ecology", "x0": 0.12981298129812982, "y0": 0.2739299610894942, "x1": 0.7909790979097909, "y1": 0.28715953307392994}, {"text": "of", "x0": 0.7964796479647965, "y0": 0.2739299610894942, "x1": 0.8140814081408141, "y1": 0.2840466926070039}, {"text": "Australia. Their population is monitored and controlled.", "x0": 0.12981298129812982, "y0": 0.29027237354085605, "x1": 0.5786578657865786, "y1": 0.3035019455252918}, {"text": "from Hawaii in 1935. The", "x0": 0.594059405940594, "y0": 0.3229571984435798, "x1": 0.801980198019802, "y1": 0.3330739299610895}, {"text": "Approximately 100 cane toads were brought to Austra", "x0": 0.12981298129812982, "y0": 0.3237354085603113, "x1": 0.5621562156215621, "y1": 0.3361867704280156}, {"text": "k is", "x0": 0.8272827282728272, "y0": 0.3408560311284047, "x1": 0.8591859185918592, "y1": 0.3610894941634241}, {"text": "number of toads has grown at a rate proportional to the population, so = kP, where", "x0": 0.12981298129812982, "y0": 0.34396887159533074, "x1": 0.823982398239824, "y1": 0.35719844357976654}, {"text": "a positive constant and P is the population.", "x0": 0.12981298129812982, "y0": 0.3649805447470817, "x1": 0.47414741474147415, "y1": 0.377431906614786}, {"text": "75 years later, in 2010, there were approximately 200 million cane toads in Australia.", "x0": 0.12981298129812982, "y0": 0.3976653696498054, "x1": 0.8162816281628162, "y1": 0.41089494163424123}, {"text": "(i) Show that P = 100e* can be used to model the population of cane toads.", "x0": 0.12981298129812982, "y0": 0.42412451361867703, "x1": 0.7513751375137514, "y1": 0.4396887159533074}, {"text": "1", "x0": 0.8844884488448845, "y0": 0.42568093385214006, "x1": 0.8921892189218922, "y1": 0.4357976653696498}, {"text": "2", "x0": 0.8833883388338833, "y0": 0.4544747081712062, "x1": 0.8932893289328933, "y1": 0.46459143968871597}, {"text": "(ii) Find the value of k. Answer correct to 2 dec